{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.Habiro.CyclotomicEvaluationRingHom","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.Habiro.CyclotomicEvaluationRingHom","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Polynomial.Eval.Defs","lean:module:Mathlib.RingTheory.Ideal.Quotient.Operations","lean:module:QOU.Habiro.CyclotomicEvaluation"],"declarations":21,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Habiro.quotientEval_bondCount","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Habiro.quotientEval_bondCount","kind":"theorem","line":305,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Habiro/CyclotomicEvaluationRingHom.lean#L305-L315","doc":"The same statement one level up, on the level-`N` truncation of the Habiro ring:\nthe rendering of a bond count whose energies are Habiro elements is a bond\ncount over `R`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Habiro.map_bondCount","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Habiro.map_bondCount","kind":"theorem","line":294,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Habiro/CyclotomicEvaluationRingHom.lean#L294-L303","doc":"**A bond count transports through the cyclotomic evaluation.** An `ℕ`-weighted\nsum of fibre-level energies renders to the `ℕ`-weighted sum of their renderings\n— i.e. the rendering of a fibre-level bond count *is* a bond count, with the\nsame counts. Every cap proved for bond counts therefore applies to it. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Habiro.habiroEval_one_ne_succ_of_not_root","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Habiro.habiroEval_one_ne_succ_of_not_root","kind":"theorem","line":267,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Habiro/CyclotomicEvaluationRingHom.lean#L267-L284","doc":"**No stabilisation off the roots of unity — so there is nothing to render.**\n\nAt a `ζ` that is not a root of unity, the all-ones cyclotomic series has a\n*different* value at every truncation level: level `N+1` differs from level `N`\nfor every `N`. `habiroEval_stable` — the well-definedness that makes `ev_ζ` a\nmap on the inverse limit at all — is therefore unavailable, and there is no\nvalue for class D to render, ring map or otherwise.\n\nThis is bean `qou-ix0x` ROAST item 4 (*\"the substrate `q₀ ≈ 1.11` is not a root\nof unity, so a cyclotomic route has to explain how root-of-unity data reaches an\nevaluation at a non-root-of-unity point\"*) answered in the negative for\nevaluation-shaped renderings: it does not reach it by evaluating. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Habiro.habiroEval_one_succ_sub","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Habiro.habiroEval_one_succ_sub","kind":"theorem","line":258,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Habiro/CyclotomicEvaluationRingHom.lean#L258-L265","doc":"Consecutive truncations of the all-ones cyclotomic series differ by exactly\n`(ζ;ζ)_N`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Habiro.qPochDiag_ne_zero_of_not_root","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Habiro.qPochDiag_ne_zero_of_not_root","kind":"theorem","line":251,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Habiro/CyclotomicEvaluationRingHom.lean#L251-L256","doc":"Contrapositive: at a non-root-of-unity `ζ` no level ever truncates. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Habiro.exists_pow_eq_one_of_qPochDiag_eq_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Habiro.exists_pow_eq_one_of_qPochDiag_eq_zero","kind":"theorem","line":240,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Habiro/CyclotomicEvaluationRingHom.lean#L240-L249","doc":"Over a domain, the truncation that makes `habiroEval` level-independent can only\nhappen at a root of unity: `(ζ;ζ)_N = 0` forces `ζ^k = 1` for some `1 ≤ k ≤ N`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Habiro.habiroPoly_one_mul","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Habiro.habiroPoly_one_mul","kind":"theorem","line":228,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Habiro/CyclotomicEvaluationRingHom.lean#L228-L236","doc":"**Anti-vacuity for `habiroEval_mul_of_repr`.** The hypothesis `hc` is\nsatisfiable: at level `1` the cyclotomic coordinates are the constant term\nalone, and the representing sequence is the plain product. Without an instance\nthe theorem above would be a statement about an empty hypothesis class. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Habiro.habiroEval_mul_of_repr","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Habiro.habiroEval_mul_of_repr","kind":"theorem","line":215,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Habiro/CyclotomicEvaluationRingHom.lean#L215-L226","doc":"**Multiplicativity of the cyclotomic evaluation**, with the Habiro product\nsupplied as a hypothesis rather than assumed as a conclusion: `hc` says that\n`c` represents the product of `a` and `b` in `R[q]/((q;q)_N)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Habiro.habiroEval_eq_quotientEval","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Habiro.habiroEval_eq_quotientEval","kind":"theorem","line":199,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Habiro/CyclotomicEvaluationRingHom.lean#L199-L204","doc":"The Habiro value at a root of unity, read off the quotient. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Habiro.cyclotomicQuotientEval_mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Habiro.cyclotomicQuotientEval_mk","kind":"theorem","line":194,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Habiro/CyclotomicEvaluationRingHom.lean#L194-L197","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Habiro.cyclotomicQuotientEval","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Habiro.cyclotomicQuotientEval","kind":"def","line":182,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Habiro/CyclotomicEvaluationRingHom.lean#L182-L192","doc":"**THE STATEMENT CLASS D NEEDS.** At a root of unity, evaluation descends to the\nlevel-`N` truncation `R[q]/((q;q)_N)` **as a ring homomorphism** — and that\ntruncation is exactly the object the Habiro ring `Ẑ[q] = lim_← R[q]/((q;q)_N)`\nis the inverse limit of.\n\nSo a rendering of a Habiro element at a root of unity is a ring map, and every\ninvariant of the form \"this quantity commutes with ring homomorphisms\"\n— `bondSum_map` in particular — transports through it unchanged. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Habiro.span_qPochPoly_le_ker","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Habiro.span_qPochPoly_le_ker","kind":"theorem","line":177,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Habiro/CyclotomicEvaluationRingHom.lean#L177-L180","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Habiro.qPochPoly_mem_ker","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Habiro.qPochPoly_mem_ker","kind":"theorem","line":171,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Habiro/CyclotomicEvaluationRingHom.lean#L171-L175","doc":"At a root of unity the evaluation kills the level-`N` Pochhammer. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Habiro.eval_qPochPoly_eq_zero_of_pow_eq_one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Habiro.eval_qPochPoly_eq_zero_of_pow_eq_one","kind":"theorem","line":166,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Habiro/CyclotomicEvaluationRingHom.lean#L166-L169","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Habiro.habiroEval_eq_cyclotomicEvalHom","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Habiro.habiroEval_eq_cyclotomicEvalHom","kind":"theorem","line":158,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Habiro/CyclotomicEvaluationRingHom.lean#L158-L164","doc":"**The Habiro coordinate map is a ring hom applied to a polynomial.**\nThis is the precise sense in which `ev_ζ` is a ring map: the non-multiplicativity\nof the cyclotomic *coordinates* is a fact about the presentation, and the\npresentation is not the map. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Habiro.cyclotomicEvalHom_apply","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Habiro.cyclotomicEvalHom_apply","kind":"theorem","line":155,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Habiro/CyclotomicEvaluationRingHom.lean#L155-L156","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Habiro.cyclotomicEvalHom","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Habiro.cyclotomicEvalHom","kind":"def","line":149,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Habiro/CyclotomicEvaluationRingHom.lean#L149-L153","doc":"Evaluation at `ζ`, **as a ring homomorphism** on `R[q]`. This is nothing but\n`Polynomial.evalRingHom`; it is named here so the class-D hypothesis can be\ndischarged by pointing at an object of type `→+*`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Habiro.eval_habiroPoly","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Habiro.eval_habiroPoly","kind":"theorem","line":140,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Habiro/CyclotomicEvaluationRingHom.lean#L140-L145","doc":"**The coordinate map factors through polynomial evaluation.** ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Habiro.habiroPoly","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Habiro.habiroPoly","kind":"def","line":136,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Habiro/CyclotomicEvaluationRingHom.lean#L136-L138","doc":"A cyclotomic series truncated at level `N`, as a polynomial. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Habiro.eval_qPochPoly","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Habiro.eval_qPochPoly","kind":"theorem","line":130,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Habiro/CyclotomicEvaluationRingHom.lean#L130-L134","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Habiro.qPochPoly","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Habiro.qPochPoly","kind":"def","line":124,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Habiro/CyclotomicEvaluationRingHom.lean#L124-L128","doc":"The diagonal `q`-Pochhammer `(q;q)_m = ∏_{k=1}^{m} (1 - q^k)` as a **polynomial**.\n`qPochDiag` is its evaluation; keeping the polynomial is what lets the whole\nconstruction be read through `Polynomial.evalRingHom`. ","signatureChunk":0}]}